# Template for results/designs.jsonl — our submission candidates.
# Copy this file to results/designs.jsonl (same folder, drop the .template) and replace the example.
# One JSON object per line. Lines starting with # and empty lines are ignored.
#
# Required keys:
#   name      letters/digits/_/-, unique, max 64 chars
#   sequence  50-260 standard uppercase amino acids
#   base      1-BASED index of the catalytic base; the residue there must be D or E
#   oxy       1-BASED index of the oxyanion-hole donor; must be Q N S T Y K or R (never H)
# Any other key (note, run, score, ...) is kept here for us and left out of the FASTA.
#
# Then run:  make submission      -> writes results/designs.fasta and checks every rule
# Details:   wiki/submission.md
#
# {"name": "chris_01", "sequence": "MKAYLVTGG...", "base": 19, "oxy": 24, "note": "run kemp-1234, seed 7"}
